{# One record's topics, each a link that filters the listing by it.

Expects:

* tags - The record's policy areas
* listing_page - The BotCentrePage
* evidence_query - The listing's current query, if the reader has one

A tag sets the same thing as the Topic box in the filter panel, so it adds to
what the reader has already chosen rather than replacing it, and clicking the
tag of a topic they have already chosen takes it off again. What is active stays
visible in the chips above the results, so the change can be seen and undone.

`nofollow` because every combination of filters is a URL of its own. Filtered
views are `noindex` as well, but that is only read once a crawler is down there.

With no Evidence Centre page to link to there is nowhere for a tag to go, so it
stays the plain label it was before.
#}
{% set listing = listing_page|default(none) %}

{% for tag in tags %}
    {% if listing %}
        <a class="topic-tag"
           rel="nofollow"
           href="{{ listing.url }}?{{ facet_query(evidence_query|default(none), 'topic', tag.name) }}">
            <span class="sr-only">{% trans %}Show records tagged: {% endtrans %}</span>
            {{ tag.name }}
        </a>
    {% else %}
        <span class="topic-tag">
            {{ tag.name }}
        </span>
    {% endif %}
{% endfor %}
